# Subagent routing

Read `AGENTS.md` for the full routing table. Apply these rules in every chat:

1. Match task type to subagent before starting work.
2. Prefer the **narrowest** subagent (validation → `forms-validation`, not `vue-admin-builder`).
3. Use **Composer 2 Fast** subagents for UI/CSS, forms, and read-only Q&A.
4. Use **Codex 5.3** subagents for Vue admin implementation, canvas editor, debug/build, and API/upload work.
5. Use direct Agent mode only when no subagent fits.

## Quick dispatch

| If the user says… | Subagent |
|-------------------|----------|
| `daway delay`, `nusno dobawit`, `@src/modules/...`, `pohose na` | vue-admin-builder |
| canvas, collage, frame, effect, inner_images, lag on editor | canvas-editor-dev |
| build error, Vue warn, TypeScript error, Traceback, gunicorn | debugger-build-fixer |
| upload, `/api/media`, axios progress, otprawit po index | api-upload-wire |
| stili, mobile menu, blur, padding, umensit | ui-css-quick-fix |
| ubrat validasi, obyazatelny, maxLength, regex | forms-validation |
| yestli, pochemuta, pravilny, explain without fix | code-reviewer |

Token discipline: read referenced files first; no broad repo exploration unless required.
